  "limits": [
    "n=2 per role/variant on one tiny held-out feature, targeted after medium-campaign failures; not a population success estimate.",
    "Offline source adjudication and three amended judge packets are post-result adaptive. Original medium and original high scores remain immutable; medium/high is not a directly paired comparison.",
    "A-dirty native UNCLEAR remains native UNCLEAR. D5 source validity is an independent root/reviewer decision in a separate layer.",
    "B pending extra concerns are not automatically false positives. One concrete B grounding defect remains regardless of pending concerns.",
    "Role adoption metadata and fresh formal executor/identity registration are separate gates; this proposal does not register a formal reviewer or mark any formal quality gate Passed.",
    "Frozen candidate harness used --setting-sources empty and strict MCP/supplied-file read-only tooling. Normal managed-launcher/settings/hooks behavior is not validated by this experiment; preserve applicable production settings/hooks/native authority.",
    "No global capability, effort support, risk floor, preference, native mapping or lifecycle change. The current registry already supports Opus/high.",
    "Candidate lifecycle requires explicit policy=pinned, model_id=anthropic/opus, requested_effort=high selection. The native mapping remains the opus alias; fresh runtime observation/delivery checks remain required.",
    "No runtime semantic-scope enforcement is added by metadata: the operator must restrict this proposed evidence-backed use to ordinary Phase-1/no-domain reviews.",
    "A future merge must union this A-only reference with separately approved self-improvement metadata, preserving PR #641 and its tests/medium support; do not replace its policy with this stable-base snapshot.",
    "Human approval activates only the stated bounded adoption metadata. It does not register a formal executor, prove a protected launch, or mark any formal review Passed. Historical evidence retains its original pre-approval statements."
  ],
